{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"USN-9094-1","published":"2026-11-16T16:24:06Z","modified":"2026-11-24T14:52:53.266206606Z","related":["UBUNTU-CVE-2026-119729","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-119842","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-85150","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-86476"],"upstream":["CVE-2026-119729","CVE-2026-119842","CVE-2026-85150","CVE-2026-86476","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-119729","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-119842","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-85150","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-86476"],"summary":"gst-plugins-bad1.0, gst-plugins-base1.0 vulnerabilities","details":"It was discovered that GStreamer did not properly handle certain RTSP\nmessages. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to cause a denial\nof service. This issue only affected Ubuntu 18.04 LTS, Ubuntu 20.04 LTS,\nUbuntu 22.04 LTS, Ubuntu 24.04 LTS, and Ubuntu 26.04 LTS.\n(CVE-2026-85150)\n\nIt was discovered that GStreamer did not properly validate video data. A\nlocal attacker could possibly use this issue to cause a denial of service\nor execute arbitrary code. This issue only affected Ubuntu 24.04 LTS,\nUbuntu 26.04 LTS, and Ubuntu 26.10.\n(CVE-2026-86476)\n\nIt was discovered that GStreamer did not properly handle certain AV1\nmedia. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to cause a denial of\nservice. This issue only affected Ubuntu 22.04 LTS and Ubuntu 24.04 LTS.\n(CVE-2026-119729)\n\nIt was discovered that GStreamer did not properly handle certain subtitle\nfiles. An attacker could possibly use this issue to cause a denial of\nservice if a user opened a specially crafted file. This issue only affected\nUbuntu 16.04 LTS, Ubuntu 18.04 LTS, Ubuntu 20.04 LTS, Ubuntu 22.04 LTS,\nand Ubuntu 24.04 LTS.\n(CVE-2026-119842)","affected":[{"package":{"name":"gst-plugins-base1.0","ecosystem":"Ubuntu:Pro:16.04:LTS","purl":"pkg:deb/ubuntu/gst-plugins-base1.0?arch=source&distro=esm-infra-legacy%2Fxenial"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"1.8.3-1ubuntu0.3+esm7"}]}],"versions":["1.6.0-1ubuntu1","1.6.1-1ubuntu1","1.6.2-1ubuntu1","1.7.1-1ubun